module haunted-house
  version: 1.0

engine-config:
  entry-scene: hall

type ItemKind = gramophone | electrical-apparatus | dusty-tome | pocket-watch | tapestry

state player:
  inventory: Set(ItemKind, 5) = (set)

fn take-item item:
  add! player/inventory item

fn collected-all?:
  count player/inventory = 5

fn has-item? item:
  contains? player/inventory item

# ─── Rooms ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

scene hall:
  The entrance hall of Ashworth Manor. Dusty portraits stare down from the walls.
  Hallways lead east to the parlour, west to the library, and north to the kitchen.

  [collected-all?] You have gathered all five strange artefacts. A faint light beckons from the front door.

  * [collected-all?] Leave the manor in triumph
    -> ending

  * Go east to the parlour
    -> parlour

  * Go west to the library
    -> library

  * Go north to the kitchen
    -> kitchen

scene parlour:
  The parlour is draped in faded red velvet. A cold hearth dominates one wall.
  A locked iron door leads down to what must be the cellar.

  [not (has-item? 'gramophone)] In the corner sits an ancient gramophone, its brass horn tarnished green.

  * [not (has-item? 'gramophone)] Take the ancient gramophone
    take-item 'gramophone
    -> parlour

  * [not (has-item? 'gramophone)] Ignore it and go back to the hall
    -> hall

  * [has-item? 'gramophone] Return to the hall
    -> hall

  * Descend to the cellar
    -> cellar

scene library:
  Floor-to-ceiling shelves sag under the weight of neglected books.
  A narrow stair at the back climbs to the attic.

  [not (has-item? 'dusty-tome)] One book lies open on the reading table: its pages are blank except for a strange symbol on the cover.

  * [not (has-item? 'dusty-tome)] Take the dusty tome
    take-item 'dusty-tome
    -> library

  * Return to the hall
    -> hall

  * Climb to the attic
    -> attic

scene kitchen:
  The kitchen smells of rust and damp. Pots hang from hooks overhead.

  [not (has-item? 'pocket-watch)] On the windowsill you notice a cracked pocket watch, its hands frozen at midnight.

  * [not (has-item? 'pocket-watch)] Take the cracked pocket watch
    take-item 'pocket-watch
    -> kitchen

  * Return to the hall
    -> hall

scene cellar:
  Cold stone walls, dripping pipes. The air hums faintly.

  [not (has-item? 'electrical-apparatus)] Against the far wall stands a mysterious electrical apparatus — coils of copper wire wound around an iron frame, purpose unknown.

  * [not (has-item? 'electrical-apparatus)] Take the mysterious electrical apparatus
    take-item 'electrical-apparatus
    -> cellar

  * Return to the parlour
    -> parlour

scene attic:
  Low rafters, cobwebs, and the faint smell of cedar.

  [not (has-item? 'tapestry)] A moth-eaten tapestry hangs from the rafters. Strange figures are woven into it.

  * [not (has-item? 'tapestry)] Take the moth-eaten tapestry
    take-item 'tapestry
    -> attic

  * Climb back down to the library
    -> library

scene ending:
  You step out of Ashworth Manor into the cold night air, arms full of inexplicable treasures.
  Behind you the front door swings shut — and locks.
  Whatever the artefacts mean, they are yours now.

  Items collected: {count player/inventory} / 5.

  * The End
    -> ending
